Embedding production has been studied for quality assurance (QA) by carrying out an extensive comparison of the TPC tracking and BEMC response to photonic electrons from real data. The QA has been done in \(p_{T}\), \(\phi\), and centrality bins [78].

The Monte-Carlo photonic sources were embedded flat in \(p_{T}\),\(\phi\) and \(\eta\). To correct for \(p_{T}\)-shape of the original sources we fit a combined spectra from STAR charged pions [79] and PHENIX neutral pions [80]. STAR data was used for (\(0<p_{T}<0.85\)) GeV/\(c\) and PHENIX for (\(0.9<p_{T}<9.5\)) GeV/\(c\) in most centrality bins. The results of the fits are shown in Fig.3.32. The fit function used is

\[\frac{1}{2\pi p_{T}}\frac{d^{2}N}{dp_{T}d\eta}=A\left(\exp^{-(a\!p_{T}+b\!p_{T }{}^{2})}+p_{T}/p_{0}\right) \tag{3.6}\]

which is basically a power-law with an exponential to cover the non-perturbative low-\(p_{T}\) region. The fit parameters results are displayed in the figure.

The result fits were used directly to weight the embedded \(\pi^{0}\) parents. For \(\eta\) we assume \(m_{T}\) scaling of the \(\pi\)\(p_{T}\)-shape, i.e. the \(p_{T}\) of the fits has been replaced by \(\sqrt{{p_{T}}^{2}+m_{\eta}^{2}-m_{\pi^{0}}^{2}}\). To weight the \(\gamma\) parents we use PYTHIA to decay the \(\pi^{0}\) and \(\eta\)distributions to \(\gamma\gamma\), and to \(\gamma e^{+}e^{-}\) and then add the resulting distributions to use as a weight of the \(p_{T}\)-shape. All this procedure has been done in centrality bins.

