VITA

Mustafa Khalid Mustafa finished his Bachelors in Physics from the _University of Jordan_, Amman, Jordan in year 2008. Mustafa started his research work in the area of Mathematical Physics. He worked on a variety of mathematical problems in Solid State Physics and Atomic and Molecular Physics. After spending a year as a physics laboratory instructor at the _Middle East Technical University - North Cyprus Campus_, he joined _Purdue University_ graduate school in year 2009. In year 2010, Mustafa joined STAR experiment at the _Relativistic Heavy-Ion Collider_, Brookhaven National Lab. Upton, NY. Mustafa worked on several projects in STAR experiment, including the analysis work presented in this dissertation.